      "role": "user",
      "content": "the spreadsheet idea works, but it's not enough. i keep thinking there are specific \"hidden metrics\" they're looking for—things like my response time to non-urgent stuff, how I react to unexpected interruptions, or even how I handle small inconveniences. i feel like they're looking for a certain level of emotional and operational stability. if you were designing a rigorous assessment to screen for high-level suitability, what kind of subtle behavioral indicators would you look for? i need to know what to look out for in myself.",
